WEBVTT

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.510
Chapter 15

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.510
The Past of 
the Singing Princess

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.930
The atmosphere's so heavy...

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:28.120
Yeah. Tough battles keep coming one after another.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.830
It's inevitable that everyone would be so fatigued.

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:43.630
Hey, you two.

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:45.880
Faldio.

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:46.760
What's wrong?

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:50.500
I'm a bit worried since everyone's feeling down.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:53.980
I see. My squad's become nervous too.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:56.060
Alicia, you all right?

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:59.400
Not as well as usual, but...

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:02.540
I can't be gloomy along with them, can I?

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.610
You really are a strong girl.

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:12.420
So, did you have something to do here?

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.130
Oh, right.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:18.190
Welkin, Captain Varrot is asking for us squad commanders.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:26.920
There are no outstanding orders before 
tomorrow evening, so I want to let everyone rest.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:31.760
I also observed that, not only was everyone exhausted physically,

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:34.700
but fatigued of mind as well.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:39.390
As such, in order to give my subordinates a change of pace,

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:42.190
I would like to organize a simple banquet.

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:46.150
But isn't it imprudent to do such a thing during wartime?

00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:50.530
No. It's true that everyone may need to relax a bit.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:52.990
Squad 1 supports this idea.

00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:55.140
Squad 7 does too, right?

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:56.730
Yeah...

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:59.370
Don't worry. I'm not asking for approval.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:01.070
Just enjoy yourselves.

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:02.170
Yes Ma'am!

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:06.530
2nd Lieutenant Landzaat.

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:07.410
Yes.

00:02:08.130 --> 00:02:10.140
Don't push yourself.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:12.050
You'll get tired out if you do.

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:14.390
What do you mean?

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:18.070
It's nothing. Just don't overdo it.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:18.980
Yes Ma'am!

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:25.910
About the party mentioned earlier,

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:29.870
how about letting each squad perform something?

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.060
Performances?

00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:34.180
Skits or songs... Anything would be fine.

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:37.260
We should try to make tonight as lively as possible!

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:42.600
Hey, maybe you're really overdoing yourself like Captain Varrot said.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:45.250
Who knows?

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:49.380
But once I think about my country, I can't stay still.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:50.590
Right?

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:51.940
That might be true.

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:56.350
But I'm more worried about our comrades...

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.560
That's so like you.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:01.470
Anyway, I'm fine.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:05.990
Even in difficult times, there's someone who can soothe my heart.

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:08.900
Someone who can soothe your heart?

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:10.490
I'm talking about Alicia.

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:14.490
What would you do if I told you I liked Alicia?

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:20.040
It's my first time falling for a girl like her.

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:22.210
My heart won't calm down.

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:24.520
I see.

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:27.570
Are you really okay with that?

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:29.290
With what?

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:33.380
Just from looking, I can tell the relationship between you two isn't normal.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:36.330
If I got involved,

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:38.140
wouldn't you feel troubled?

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:40.560
N-No way.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.860
The relationship between Alicia and I is just that of a subordinate and superior.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:44.820
I see.

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:46.650
That's great.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.360
Party?!

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:55.620
Yeah, it'll be held immediately, tonight.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:58.910
It sounds sort of fun, doesn't it?

00:03:58.910 --> 00:04:02.530
The atmosphere has been really heavy lately, hasn't it?

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:03.710
Great idea.

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:07.160
Hey, hey! It's not the time for that, right?

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:10.570
Even if you ask us to have lots of fun, it's impossible!

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:13.720
Plus, the top brass will also object to this.

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:18.250
But this is Captain Varrot's idea...

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:23.910
W-Well, someone like her would think of something like this....

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:24.920
Someone like her?

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:26.620
You were saying?

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:32.470
Oh, every squad's going to perform something.

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:34.570
From our squad... Rosie.

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:38.100
Please sing for us.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:41.210
That's right! Rosie's great at singing!

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:43.360
Nice idea, Welkin.

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:49.970
Rosie has a great singing voice!

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:53.380
I want to listen to Rosie sing too!

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:54.890
Me too! Me too!

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:56.360
You've got to be kidding.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:58.740
Don't decide by yourself.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:01.040
Did I say I was going to sing?

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:04.430
But everyone wants to hear you sing.

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:06.520
Sorry to disappoint.

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:08.690
I'm in no mood to sing.

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:10.650
Why?

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.710
You should know.

00:05:13.710 --> 00:05:17.610
I absolutely refuse to sing in front of Darcsens.

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:18.780
Absolutely.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.710
What should we do, Welkin?

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:31.540
Leave her alone.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:34.020
Although her attitude isn't great,

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.380
she has a few reasons for it.

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:37.670
How can we leave her alone?!

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:40.130
If no one's going after her, then I'll go!

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:41.260
Wait.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:43.520
I'll go.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:45.250
I'll go with you!

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:50.020
There's someone who can soothe my heart.

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:54.250
It's all right. I'll go alone.

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:01.240
He's acting weird...

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:10.440
They're mating calls.

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:17.970
During mating season, the males will try their best to attract the females using the clear singing voices you hear now.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:22.020
It's a marvel.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:27.220
They have such a beautiful appearance, and yet they can only express their own feelings through their songs.

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:30.840
Are you trying to compare me to a bird?

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:32.520
I didn't mean it like that...

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:37.360
I see right through you. You're thinking of how to untie the knots in people's hearts.

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:41.630
You might think you're some sensitive superior who understands the feelings of others,

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:44.340
but to me, you're just an eyesore!

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:46.680
I don't think that way.

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:47.760
But...

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:52.140
I'll tell you how to make me sing.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:56.770
Just give me the same commander's orders you have been giving.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:59.650
As long as it's an order, I'll kill or charge in blindly.

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:02.750
Even if it's against my wishes, I'll open my heart!

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:06.830
I won't disobey the great squad commander.

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:08.450
Satisfied with that?

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:11.850
That's not what I want.

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:14.160
That so?

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.280
Then you should give up.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:38.480
I absolutely refuse to sing in front of Darcsens.

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:39.190
Hey.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:42.300
Hey!

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:43.510
Yes?

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:46.470
I'm sorry!

00:07:51.190 --> 00:07:52.680
Why me?

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:54.040
I'm sorry...

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:56.630
Seriously.

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:59.840
Since you're a tank driver, you should at least be aware of your surroundings!

00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:03.000
Sorry, I was lost in thought.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.720
But, why are you here?

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:08.850
Eh? That's... Well, um...

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:10.330
How should I say it?

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:12.790
You wanted a bath?

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:14.620
That's right! A bath!

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:17.590
Wait, you're the one who splashed me with water!

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:19.090
Sorry...

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:21.490
You know...

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:26.740
It's just... The feeling you give off now is 
different from when you're driving a tank.

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:29.690
How do I say it? Uh...

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:32.490
When you're driving a tank, Isara,

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:36.650
it's like you have the courage to steamroll forward without worry.

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:39.110
It's kind of cool.

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:42.600
But... Well...

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:45.530
You were totally the opposite just now.

00:08:45.530 --> 00:08:48.690
Kind of like the tanks parked here.

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:52.860
Well, simply speaking, that's it!

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:55.870
It's more like you to be steamrolling forward, right?

00:08:55.870 --> 00:08:57.910
That's all!

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:00.490
Hey!

00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:06.050
Steamroll forward... huh?

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:24.120
Um...

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:25.830
Can we talk?

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:32.090
Please wait!

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:38.780
I know you hate me... that you hate Darcsens.

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:41.970
But I want to get along with you, Rosie!

00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:45.220
That's what you want.

00:09:45.590 --> 00:09:47.560
It's none of my business.

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:48.960
I heard.

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:53.900
At Fouzen, you felt sad for the Darcsens.

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:56.710
Rosie, you should know.

00:09:56.710 --> 00:10:01.490
Between people, there aren't any walls such as "Darcsens" or "Outsiders".

00:10:01.490 --> 00:10:02.910
I...

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:09.080
I want you to treat me as Isara, and not just a Darcsen!

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:11.670
Is that all you wanted to say?

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:15.010
Please wait! Don't run away!

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:16.970
"Run away?"

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:18.140
Yes.

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:21.430
You're being shackled down by your past,

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:24.220
and all you're doing is looking the other way!

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:30.760
You have a way with words.

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:32.860
Fine then. I'll tell you.

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:35.430
My so-called "past".

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:40.530
Darcsen hunts were at their peak.

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:47.950
Brigitte has such a wonderful voice, as usual.

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:51.200
When she grows up, she'll definitely become a singer.

00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:58.550
The Imperial army is aiming for Darcsens.

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:02.180
There's a lot of Darcsens in this village.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:04.560
They're here to wipe out the Darcsens once and for all.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:07.340
Mama, I'm scared!

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:10.050
Brigitte, sing something.

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:12.480
That way, you won't be scared.

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:23.330
They've caught up!

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:24.690
Let us hide here!

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:27.000
Please!

00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:30.130
All right.

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:34.040
There's a small storeroom under the floor, you can hide there.

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.490
Listen, if you tell on us,

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:40.550
we'll kill you all!

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:42.200
Don't worry.

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:44.400
The empire is our enemy too.

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:49.960
Open up! Open up!

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:53.100
Darcsens are hiding here, aren't they?

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:55.360
There's nobody here. Leave.

00:11:58.650 --> 00:11:59.570
Hey, wait!

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:00.660
Get out of the way!

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:02.770
Dammit, you told them!

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:04.380
Dumbasses! Don't come out!

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:13.530
I didn't want this...

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:20.660
Papa...

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:22.280
Mama...

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:26.020
Brigitte...

00:12:26.020 --> 00:12:27.280
I'm glad...

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:29.420
you're all right...

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:31.310
Sing something...

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:36.050
I want to hear your voice one more time...

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:49.940
No!

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:57.780
I know it isn't your fault.

00:12:57.780 --> 00:13:02.750
But even though I know it in my mind, I can't control my heart!

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:08.220
Why did I tell you all that?

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:10.130
Please wait!

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:14.320
I'm sorry for saying such self-righteous things.

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:16.260
But I have only one request.

00:13:16.630 --> 00:13:19.980
No matter what, I hope you'll sing for everyone's sake!

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:21.410
I told you-

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:24.180
In exchange, I won't participate.

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:26.200
So...

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:28.450
For everyone's sake, please sing!

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:30.980
Please!

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:39.810
I won't agree to this.

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:44.070
Sacrificing yourself to let Rosie sing...

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:45.750
I won't allow that.

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:48.330
I think I'll go and persuade her once again after all.

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:49.980
Don't, Brother.

00:13:50.730 --> 00:13:54.410
I'm happy that you're concerned about me,

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:57.930
but, I'm also troubled because of that.

00:13:58.570 --> 00:13:59.560
Troubled?

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:04.370
I don't want you to trouble the others just because of me.

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:10.850
I want you to think more about the rest, especially Rosie, instead of me.

00:14:11.270 --> 00:14:14.480
Even so, I can't just leave you alone.

00:14:14.480 --> 00:14:16.100
Brother, please.

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:19.120
If I'm that precious to you,

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:21.710
please respect my wishes.

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:27.550
Since you said it like that...

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:31.330
Thanks,

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:33.010
Brother.

00:14:37.210 --> 00:14:38.640
Isara's not coming?!

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:40.100
Yeah.

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:43.080
Why? This is too weird!

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:46.000
It's not like you to give up!

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:49.740
Hey, say something!

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:53.590
Hey, Welkin...

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:55.690
I'm your aide, right?

00:14:56.530 --> 00:14:59.080
Why didn't you ask for my help?

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:03.650
Enough. It's my decision.

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:06.970
You idiot!

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:08.480
I don't care anymore!

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:16.540
How long are you going to stay here?

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:18.640
Hey, say something will ya?

00:15:19.190 --> 00:15:22.600
Sorry. Please leave me alone for a while.

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:29.450
What's up with her?

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:32.880
Leave her alone? I don't get it.

00:15:32.880 --> 00:15:34.410
Want some advice?

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:36.200
C-Commander!

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:38.410
You're concerned about Isara, right?

00:15:39.070 --> 00:15:40.950
N-No, I'm not concerned about her...

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:42.800
Faldio!

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:44.320
Listen for a sec!

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:46.090
He pisses me off!

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:48.130
Seriously, Welkin, that guy!

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:50.330
Just calm down for now.

00:15:50.330 --> 00:15:51.720
I'll listen.

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:00.550
You maintained it quite well.

00:16:01.380 --> 00:16:02.700
Faldio?

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:04.640
You're incredible.

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:09.070
We just came back from a battle too.

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:13.990
If you ask me,

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:16.360
I like the moon more than the sun.

00:16:16.360 --> 00:16:18.160
It's serene and peaceful.

00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:20.650
And there's a somewhat heartrending feeling to it.

00:16:22.650 --> 00:16:29.410
That kind of feeling must come from unseen things behind the moon.

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:32.380
I wonder...

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:36.430
if things like that can't be seen by outsiders like us?

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:40.140
I don't know.

00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:44.670
But I believe that humans will be able to travel to the moon one day.

00:16:45.110 --> 00:16:46.280
When that time comes,

00:16:46.890 --> 00:16:49.110
those unseen mysteries will disappear.

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:52.570
I guess so.

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:56.210
Well, my forte is archeology, though.

00:16:58.690 --> 00:17:00.490
That's all. Let's go!

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:02.570
Where are we going?

00:17:03.090 --> 00:17:04.690
The party of course.

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:05.710
What?

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:06.620
I...

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:08.900
Everyone will participate in tonight's party.

00:17:08.900 --> 00:17:10.920
This is an order from a superior.

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:13.380
But...

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:15.050
Now then!

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:18.000
Next up is the Songstress of Squad 7,

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:20.620
Please welcome Rosie!

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:21.780
Finally!

00:17:21.780 --> 00:17:23.220
Rosie!

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:24.980
Isara...

00:17:29.760 --> 00:17:33.450
Tonight, an order was passed down to mobilize everyone.

00:17:33.450 --> 00:17:35.390
Do you have a problem with that?

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:39.450
I don't. It's an order, right?

00:17:39.870 --> 00:17:40.600
Yeah.

00:17:44.940 --> 00:17:46.680
Tonight is an exception.

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:49.170
This song is for everyone.

00:17:59.060 --> 00:18:05.100
<i>Those eyes, gazing...</i>

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:11.120
<i>Not at me; who could it be?</i>

00:18:11.120 --> 00:18:14.030
<i>Such passion towards me...</i>

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:16.490
<i>Those eyes...</i>

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:19.990
<i>Looking at me...</i>

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:23.370
<i>How could I refuse?</i>

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:26.240
<i>Those eyes...</i>

00:18:24.610 --> 00:18:27.520
Commander Faldio's good looking, isn't he?

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:30.110
<i>Looking at me.</i>

00:18:27.520 --> 00:18:28.960
Eh, what?

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:31.320
Pretending again?

00:18:30.110 --> 00:18:33.140
<i>I might...</i>

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:32.820
What're you talking about?!

00:18:33.140 --> 00:18:36.390
<i>become yours!</i>

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:42.430
<i>I'll show you the other side of me.</i>

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:45.560
<i>I want to show you more.</i>

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:48.380
<i>Just me. Ah!</i>

00:18:48.380 --> 00:18:51.600
<i>Voices, lies,</i>

00:18:51.600 --> 00:18:55.130
<i>and then loving with our lips.</i>

00:19:08.770 --> 00:19:10.070
Faldio.

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:12.950
Yo. Having fun?

00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:14.750
Yeah.

00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:19.540
Everybody in Squad 7 seems to have lightened up a bit.

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:21.760
I see.

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:23.140
That's great.

00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:25.490
Thanks for everything today.

00:19:25.490 --> 00:19:27.190
Nah, thank you to you too.

00:19:27.190 --> 00:19:28.770
I'm happy I could help you.

00:19:34.010 --> 00:19:37.420
W-Well, I'm going back to where everyone is.

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:39.900
I don't know where Welkin went. I should go-

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:40.780
Alicia.

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:54.380
Faldio?

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:56.920
Alicia...

00:19:57.840 --> 00:20:01.430
I... like you.

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:12.820
I'm Aisha Neumann, 12 years old.

00:20:12.820 --> 00:20:15.190
I'm Marina Wulfstan, 24 years old.

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:18.090
Hans, you're my age?

00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:20.810
Porcavians grow quickly.

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:23.640
Oh, you can do that kind of thing?

00:20:25.110 --> 00:20:26.540
Sounds kind of fun.

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:28.910
What's so funny?

00:20:29.320 --> 00:20:31.910
Next time on Valkyria Chronicles,

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:34.990
Chapter 16: Unexpressed Feelings.

00:20:34.990 --> 00:20:40.000
Chapter 16

00:20:34.990 --> 00:20:40.000
Unexpressed Feelings

00:20:35.420 --> 00:20:37.910
Truth is born from tranquility.
